Venetium 0073 - a GitHub update check every 7 days.
At browser start, when the last successful check is 7 days old or more, Venetium waits a minute and then asks GitHub's
public releases API for the latest stable release of hamed7ir/venetium (one GET, no cookies; prereleases are not
"latest"). If its tag (like v1.5) is newer than this build's, an infobar says "Venetium v1.5 is available (you have
v1.4)." with a Download link to the release page; it stays until closed. Offline or rate limited: try again at the next
start. This build's tag comes from the GN arg venetium_release_tag (set in the venetium args; empty = no check), via a
small generated header, so a new tag rebuilds one file. Switches: --disable-venetium-update-check (off),
--venetium-update-check-now (ignore the 7 days, check after 3 s), --venetium-update-check-tag=vX.Y (compare as if this
build were vX.Y, to see the infobar). The infobar reuses the Windows 10 banner's id, which 0072 retired.

